  20: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  21:     """
  22:     Extract the unique foreground color mask whose cropped shape is symmetric across a vertical axis.
  23: 
  24:     Input structure:
  25:     - The grid has a dominant background and several colored masks.
  26:     - Each non-background color forms one candidate mask, possibly split into multiple 4-connected objects.
  27:     - Exactly one candidate's bounding-box crop is invariant under left-right reflection.
  28: 
  29:     Rule:
  30:     - For each non-background color, crop all pixels of that color to their bounding box.
  31:     - Select the unique crop that equals its left-right mirror image.
  32:     - Return that crop, with non-selected cells in the crop set to the background color.
  33: 
  34:     Key insight:
  35:     - The target is not identified by its color or size; it is the only color mask with vertical mirror symmetry.
